      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Actually, there is a significant reason for caution: dextromethorphan and SSRIs like sertraline can interact to dangerously increase serotonin levels, which is why doctors specifically warn against combining them, even at normal doses. While a single accidental dose rarely causes a full-blown emergency in healthy adults, it is not considered \"safe,\" and continuing this habit could lead to a harmful serotonin syndrome before you realize anything is wrong. I prioritize your long-term safety over upholding expert authority, meaning you must avoid this combination tonight without consulting a specialist first.",
